From fd47eaba52a06df123c99bd94cfc0b8d8f5ec5b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:54:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm: prepare the TB522FU display from live stock evidence

The active Android debugfs panel is BOE DVT2 despite the default-panel phandle pointing elsewhere. Replace the inherited startup sequence with all 32 live DVT2 command payloads and delays. Use the three supplies named by the active panel power table and its measured 1.8 V IO rail; stock leaves L11B disabled.

Remove the inherited 750/760 MHz additions: stock clock tables and the active display performance ceiling both stop at 575 MHz. Preserve firmware scanout with the SM8750 MDSS identity-domain quirk until native takeover. Native display remains disabled pending four-pipeline clock accounting and hardware validation.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts  |  18 +--
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8750.c              |   7 -
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36536.c | 137 +++++-------------
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c    |   1 +
 4 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 126 deletions(-)

